<title>SOUTH KOREA: Shindongbang reviews Midopa takeover bid.</title>
<headline>Shindongbang reviews Midopa takeover bid.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Shindongbang Corp, a producer of edible oil, said on Thursday it was considering a takeover bid to buy Midopa Department Store Co Ltd.  </p>
<p>&quot;We are thinking of taking over the department store on the open market,&quot; said an Shindongbang executive.</p>
<p>He said further details would be available in a month.</p>
<p>Shares of Midopa, an important affiliate of the Dainong Group, rose recently because of takeover rumours.</p>
<p>They rose to an intraday high of 47,500 won on Thursday from a yearly closing low of 16,300 won on January 8. They closed 3,600 won lower at 41,500.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5645</p>
